  "step_3": "The decision reason is based on skewness — specifically, preferring the lottery with a greater probability mass on unfavorable outcomes (i.e., more right-skewed). In this case, Lottery B has a 99.9% chance of 0 Euros, making it slightly more right-skewed than A (99.8%). The reason would therefore prefer B. However, the verbal report does not mention skewness, distribution shape, or any comparison of the probability weight on unfavorable outcomes. Instead, the individual justifies the choice by minimizing losses — a different reasoning principle (risk aversion or loss minimization), not skewness. There is no indication that the individual considered or applied the rule about skewness. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
